WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:09.334
LIRIL is the neural processing unit at the core of TENET5 — the ethics gate that classifies every record in The 504 Database before any other system touches it.

00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:23.022
Operating at seed value one hundred and eighteen thousand four hundred, LIRIL has classified one thousand one hundred and five government accountability records across six categories using deterministic keyword analysis, source verification, and severity assessment.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:32.784
Every classification is baked at build time, not generated dynamically — ensuring that when LIRIL flags a record as critical, that judgment is reproducible, auditable, and permanent.
